    "annotations": [
      {
        "id": "a1",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Plant.** The body is a full 6-DOF `Free3D` + `RigidBody3D` bond graph that carries the whole robot's mass and inertia with the legs locked in the stance. The eight legs `Leg1`..`Leg8` are instances of one library subsystem, `SpiderLegUnit`: the leg IK, the reduced three-joint leg (`SpiderLeg`: servo angle dynamics, link gravity, foot contact) and its wrench on the body. The leg is quasi-static and signal-coupled: the body feels it only through the contact force at the foot and the moment of the link weights; the servo reactions and the inertia of a swinging leg do not reach the body (see the README).",
        "x": 40,
        "y": -120,
        "w": 1800,
        "h": 90,
        "color": "blue"
      },
      {
        "id": "a2",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Gait and control.** `Gait` is the T8X Bigfoot-style layer: an alternating tetrapod with a constant-speed stance (70 % of the cycle) and a Hermite swing, and a filtered roll/pitch correction of the foot targets (the height loop is off). Inside each leg, `IK` turns the body-frame foot target into three joint commands and `Joints` adds the servo (HS-82MG class: P loop, stall torque, back-EMF), the link weights, the contact force and the wrench on the body. `IK` and `Joints` use the same kinematic chain as the 3D scene.",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 520,
        "w": 1800,
        "h": 90,
        "color": "green"
      }
    ]
  },
